WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:09.923
My name is Maria,

00:00:09.923 --> 00:00:11.214
and I'm going to walk you through

00:00:11.214 --> 00:00:14.035
on how I restored my Barbie's plane.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.114
What makes this plane very special

00:00:18.114 --> 00:00:20.060
is that they don't do

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.130
more of these planes anymore.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:26.470
So it's an old plane that's 21 years old.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:29.012
The plane was in really bad conditions.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.036
The first thing I'm going to clean

00:00:33.036 --> 00:00:35.370
is the inside of the plane.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.930
The color of the plane
was originally blue,

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:42.740
but you can tell there's
some yellowish around

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.420
because it's too old.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.803
The best way to clean the plane,

00:00:46.803 --> 00:00:50.036
it will be doing circular motion

00:00:50.036 --> 00:00:51.830
with the toothbrush.

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:54.930
That way, everything starts to come off.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.260
And because I'm using the dish soap,

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:59.709
if there's something greasy on the plane,

00:00:59.709 --> 00:01:01.684
it's going to take it off.

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:07.562
The biggest issue with
restoring this plane

00:01:07.562 --> 00:01:09.053
are the stickers,

00:01:09.053 --> 00:01:13.060
because you can barely
see what is on them.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:14.668
For removing the stickers,

00:01:14.668 --> 00:01:16.540
I'm going to use this red spatula

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:19.131
that is made of plastic silicone,

00:01:19.131 --> 00:01:21.689
and very gently I'm going to go

00:01:21.689 --> 00:01:23.597
through the windows

00:01:23.597 --> 00:01:27.830
and all the parts that
have sticker residue.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:29.511
It's extremely important

00:01:29.511 --> 00:01:33.150
that we remove completely every residue.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:37.130
If not, the primer will not stick well,

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.738
and we're going to see

00:01:38.738 --> 00:01:41.150
painting of the primer breaking,

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:43.933
and then not even the sandpaper

00:01:43.933 --> 00:01:45.041
is going to take that out.

00:01:45.041 --> 00:01:48.865
So we have to be very,
very careful in this part.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.710
After cleaning and
removing all the stickers,

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:00.480
it's very important to put this primer

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.060
before the spray paint,
because this is going to

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:06.383
let the other paint
just stick much better.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.980
We don't want to spray a
lot of layers on the plane.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:15.810
Otherwise it wouldn't
open well or track well.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:18.270
We're just going to put two coats.

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:21.528
One, the primer, and then the spray paint.

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.123
The reason why I chose the spray paint

00:02:28.123 --> 00:02:31.430
is because it sticks
very well on the plastic.

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:32.755
The spray technique,

00:02:32.755 --> 00:02:35.471
it's pretty much just going from afar,

00:02:35.471 --> 00:02:39.040
never close, and from left to right.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:41.661
Very patient, so it doesn't drip.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.851
The plane originally is made of plastic,

00:02:45.851 --> 00:02:48.070
and it has no paint.

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:50.137
The plastic was originally blue.

00:02:50.137 --> 00:02:51.887
So it was a challenge, because it's not

00:02:51.887 --> 00:02:54.670
going to be 100% how it was before,

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:57.428
but it's going to be very, very close.

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:00.696
For the pink chairs,

00:03:00.696 --> 00:03:03.687
I'm going to mix two
colors, white and red,

00:03:03.687 --> 00:03:05.800
and then I'm going to
put it in an airbrusher

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:08.700
so I can spray them all around.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.112
What is going to take me most of the time

00:03:20.112 --> 00:03:24.430
is actually doing or
rebuilding the stickers.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:27.690
I was trying to find
the stickers everywhere,

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:30.900
websites, internet, and
I couldn't find anything,

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:34.020
so that's why I decided
to do it by myself.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.860
I had to print them in
two different papers.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:40.260
The first, it's going to
be on a white background.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:41.412
That was very useful

00:03:41.412 --> 00:03:44.036
for the stickers that were on the windows,

00:03:44.036 --> 00:03:45.428
the ones in the tail

00:03:45.428 --> 00:03:48.060
that has the Barbie logo and everything.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.701
And then for the flowers,

00:03:49.701 --> 00:03:51.749
because the blue behind the flowers

00:03:51.749 --> 00:03:53.999
was the original blue,

00:03:53.999 --> 00:03:56.348
it was really hard to match

00:03:56.348 --> 00:03:58.230
the spray paint that I used.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:01.438
So I just went through a
transparent background,

00:04:01.438 --> 00:04:03.521
so you can see the flowers

00:04:03.521 --> 00:04:05.320
but you can also see through them

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:10.230
and see this beautiful new
blue from the spray paint.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:15.060
To remember how or where
to put all these stickers

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:17.193
and not to miss anything,

00:04:17.193 --> 00:04:19.368
I want to say I looked to the pictures

00:04:19.368 --> 00:04:20.610
and I made my research,

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:23.396
but honestly I played
so much with this plane

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:25.422
that it was all in my mind

00:04:25.422 --> 00:04:28.130
and I knew exactly which stickers

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:31.522
I had to make or where to put them.

